# Wedge product path

Canonical docs: `docs/product/overview.md`, `docs/product/roadmap.md`, `docs/product/phases/v*.md`.

## What Wedge is

macOS **menu-bar only** utility (OneThing-adjacent). The bar shows the **one thing** (list index 0). Everything else is **Up next**, ordered by drag. Position = priority — no priority fields. **Done** (pop + sound) is the emotional core.

## Language

**one thing** · **Up next** · **Done** — not push/pop/stack/P0. Empty bar: **icon only**. Non-empty: **title only** (no circle).

## Horizon

**v1 → v2 → v3 only.** No v4. No cloud/sync/accounts. No Dock mode. No confetti.

## v1 (current build target)

- Compact floating **panel** on left click (centered on screen, add field focused; window title **Wedge**); single list with Notion-style **6-dot drag grips**; add always to bottom of Up next.
- Done: ⌘↩ (panel key), ⌥+click, right-click menu (no Force-click; no panel Done button).
- Persist locally. **Launch at login.**
- **Max 40 characters** per item; enforce limit; **no truncation/ellipsis logic**.
- **Minimal Settings:** native **⌘,** / **Settings…** (panel open or status-item menu). Menu-bar one-thing **bold** + **color** (Automatic = system label, or custom). More prefs in v3.
- See `docs/product/phases/v1.md`.

## Later (do not build early)

- v2: global hotkeys + denser panel keyboard — `phases/v2.md`
- v3: expand Settings (sound, login control, hotkey remap) — `phases/v3.md`

## Alignment

On any confirmed product change, update the matching phase doc + this rule (`wedge-keep-aligned`).
